          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %em Cayley distance
            between two
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/permutations"} permutations
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/minimum"} minimum
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+number"} number
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transpositions"} transpositions
            of elements needed to turn one into the other.
          %p
            (This is in contrast to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kendall+distance"} Kendall distance
            which counts the minimum number of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transpositions"} transpositions
            of
            %em adjacent
            pairs of elements.)
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
          #CayleyDistance.num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              %strong (Cayley distance)
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              consider the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+group"} symmetric group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Sym
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sym(n)
              with its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mathematical+structure"} structure
              as a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finitely+generated+group"} finitely generated group
              exhibited by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+set"} finite set
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generators"} generators
              given by all
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transposition+permutations"} transposition permutations
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Gen
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi σ
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ,
                        %mi j
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi i
                    %mo ,
                    %mi j
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} }
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi Sym
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Gen
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    \\big\{
                    \\sigma_{i,j}
                    \\,\vert\,
                    1 \leq i, j \lt n
                    \\big\}
                    \\;\subset\;
                    Sym(n)
                    \\,.
            %p
              Then the
              %em Cayley distance
              (e.g
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "#Diaconis88"} Diaconis 88, p. 112
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distance"} distance
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Sym
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sym(n)
              which is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graph+distance"} graph distance
              of the corresponding
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cayley+graph"} Cayley graph
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi Sym
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Sym
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi ℕ
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    d_C(-,-)
                    \\;\colon\;
                    Sym(n) \times Sym(n)
                    \\longrightarrow
                    \\mathbb{N}
                    \\hookrightarrow
                    \\mathbb{R}
            %p
              which sends any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pair"} pair
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/permutations"} permutations
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi σ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi σ
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Sym
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma_1, \sigma_2 \in Sym(n)
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/minimum"} minimum
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/number"} number
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi σ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi σ
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d(\sigma_1, \sigma_2) \in \mathbb{N}
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transpositions"} transpositions
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi σ
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi i
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi j
                          %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi σ
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi i
                          %mn 2
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi j
                          %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi σ
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi i
                          %mi d
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi j
                          %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma_{i_1, j_1}, \sigma_{i_2, j_2}, \cdots, \sigma_{i_d, j_d}
              such that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi σ
                      %mn 2
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi σ
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi i
                          %mi d
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi j
                          %mi d
